WEBVTT

00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:25.920
Ready? While you're being swarmed,
I'll take down the main enemy.

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:27.210
Hey, legendary detective,

00:00:27.210 --> 00:00:29.720
don't devise a plan that treats
my death as a foregone conclusion.

00:00:29.720 --> 00:00:30.760
It's all right.

00:00:30.760 --> 00:00:34.810
I'll take responsibility and delete
your computer's search history.

00:00:34.810 --> 00:00:41.270
Wait a minute! Hey, you saw it?
You looked at my search history?

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:47.030
After I became sidekick to Siesta, a
detective who battled humanity's enemies,

00:00:47.030 --> 00:00:51.990
our adventure drama together unfolded
over the course of three years.

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:58.160
It's been a year since those
dizzying days came to an end.

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:02.540
As a high-school senior, I have immersed
myself from head to toe, wholeheartedly,

00:01:02.540 --> 00:01:07.670
in the lukewarm water
I now call "everyday life."

00:01:07.670 --> 00:01:14.180
Is it enough, you ask? It is;
this life of mine impinges on nobody.

00:01:14.180 --> 00:01:19.890
That's how it is... since the
detective is already dead.

00:01:21.850 --> 00:01:24.060
You're the legendary detective?

00:02:58.570 --> 00:03:03.830
I am presently being threatened
by a girl I've never seen before.

00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:03.910
Episode 2

00:03:04.120 --> 00:03:06.920
What's more, the reason
is completely unclear.

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:09.500
Don't keep quiet; answer me.

00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:11.500
Are you Kimihiko Kimizuka,

00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:14.050
the legendary detective
I've heard rumors about?

00:03:14.050 --> 00:03:19.260
Detective... It's a disagreeable word
that I haven't heard in a year.

00:03:19.260 --> 00:03:21.470
You have the wrong person. Now excuse me.

00:03:21.470 --> 00:03:22.970
Wait!

00:03:23.890 --> 00:03:29.480
If you won't give me a proper answer,
I'll touch your uvula, without mercy.

00:03:29.480 --> 00:03:32.150
You're Kimihiko Kimizuka, aren't you?

00:03:32.150 --> 00:03:33.150
Mm-hrrrm.

00:03:33.150 --> 00:03:35.820
Speak up when you answer!

00:03:36.990 --> 00:03:38.780
Eww, you're the worst--

00:03:38.780 --> 00:03:43.660
getting all this drool on the fingers
of a girl you just met.

00:03:43.660 --> 00:03:49.580
What is with this absurd behavior?
What on Earth am I being punished for?

00:03:49.580 --> 00:03:53.050
Oh, hold on. That's what it is.

00:03:58.260 --> 00:04:01.220
You wanted to be hugged.

00:04:08.980 --> 00:04:12.900
No, no, no, no, no!
What are you trying to do here?

00:04:12.900 --> 00:04:17.150
Too bad. We could have
had a little more fun.

00:04:17.150 --> 00:04:19.490
Don't throw your body around
so much to "have fun."

00:04:19.490 --> 00:04:22.700
Don't offer up your chest
to some guy you don't know.

00:04:26.750 --> 00:04:29.080
Nagisa Natsunagi.

00:04:31.210 --> 00:04:34.090
Could I ask you to clean off
your hand first?

00:04:36.550 --> 00:04:40.340
I came here with a request for you.

00:04:41.550 --> 00:04:47.430
I'm looking for someone.
You're... the legendary detective, right?

00:04:47.430 --> 00:04:49.690
Unfortunately, you've
got the wrong person.

00:04:49.690 --> 00:04:51.350
The wrong person?

00:04:54.440 --> 00:04:56.320
"Direct-Deposit Scammer Gang Apprehended,"

00:04:56.320 --> 00:04:59.780
"High-School Hero,"
"A Pro at Finding Lost Pets,"

00:04:59.780 --> 00:05:02.450
"Surprise Interview with the Boy Named K."

00:05:02.450 --> 00:05:04.950
"Boy Hero Saves Lives."

00:05:04.950 --> 00:05:10.410
If you still insist you're not a legendary
detective, just what <i>are </i>you?

00:05:13.460 --> 00:05:15.670
You said you're looking for someone?

00:05:15.670 --> 00:05:18.880
Will you be the detective for my case?

00:05:18.880 --> 00:05:22.130
I'll never be a detective. However...

00:05:22.130 --> 00:05:23.840
However?

00:05:23.840 --> 00:05:26.260
If a sidekick will suffice,
I'll take the case.

00:05:26.260 --> 00:05:28.140
What does that mean?

00:05:28.140 --> 00:05:31.390
So who are you looking for?

00:05:32.810 --> 00:05:39.400
I want you... I want you to find out
who it is I'm trying to find.

00:05:39.400 --> 00:05:40.900
Huh?

00:05:44.740 --> 00:05:49.290
There's somebody I absolutely
need to meet and talk to...

00:05:49.290 --> 00:05:53.170
But I have absolutely no idea who it is.

00:05:53.170 --> 00:05:59.510
I don't have even the vaguest guess about
their age, gender, or where they live.

00:05:59.510 --> 00:06:05.300
Let's call this unknown individual you're
searching for "X," for the time being.

00:06:05.300 --> 00:06:08.810
Don't you know anything about X?

00:06:08.810 --> 00:06:14.100
I don't. I don't even understand
why I'm preoccupied with X.

00:06:14.100 --> 00:06:19.150
There are just these sudden moments
when I want to meet X.

00:06:19.150 --> 00:06:22.320
And approximately when did this start?

00:06:22.320 --> 00:06:24.320
One year ago.

00:06:24.320 --> 00:06:27.280
What happened one year ago?

00:06:27.280 --> 00:06:34.250
I was on the verge of death when I got
my life back. No, I was <i>given </i>life.

00:06:34.250 --> 00:06:39.090
The heartbeat I had you listen to
in the classroom... it's not my own.

00:06:39.090 --> 00:06:42.510
You had... a heart transplant.

00:06:42.510 --> 00:06:45.550
I had a serious heart condition ever since
I was little, and was constantly

00:06:45.550 --> 00:06:47.760
in and out of hospitals,
all the while waiting for the day

00:06:47.760 --> 00:06:49.760
I could get a transplant.

00:06:49.760 --> 00:06:53.600
One year ago, a suitable donor
was found at last,

00:06:53.600 --> 00:06:56.940
and I was able to undergo
the heart transplant procedure.

00:06:56.940 --> 00:07:02.480
Ever since then, X's existence
began to flit through my brain.

00:07:02.480 --> 00:07:06.410
I see. It's memory transference.

00:07:06.410 --> 00:07:07.410
Huh?

00:07:07.410 --> 00:07:13.540
The X you're looking for is a person whom
the heart's original owner wants to see.

00:07:13.540 --> 00:07:14.750
That's the most ridiculous--

00:07:14.750 --> 00:07:21.000
If you think so, why did you tell me
about your heart transplant?

00:07:21.000 --> 00:07:25.550
Although the phenomenon of memory
transference isn't scientifically proven,

00:07:25.550 --> 00:07:28.180
there have been a number of
cases where, after surgery,

00:07:28.180 --> 00:07:30.510
the recipient was influenced
by the organ donor:

00:07:30.510 --> 00:07:32.930
Starting to like foods they'd hated,

00:07:32.930 --> 00:07:37.020
having memories of places
they'd never even visited...

00:07:37.020 --> 00:07:38.190
So, what?

00:07:38.190 --> 00:07:43.360
You're saying it's not that I want to
meet X, but rather this heart does?

00:07:43.360 --> 00:07:49.240
Probably. So X is most likely someone
close to the donor while they were alive--

00:07:49.240 --> 00:07:54.410
a family member, a lover, a friend...

00:07:54.410 --> 00:07:56.370
Really...

00:07:56.370 --> 00:08:01.880
Well, I'm glad it was only that.
So that wraps up this problem.

00:08:01.880 --> 00:08:04.250
Huh? Where are you going?

00:08:04.250 --> 00:08:06.260
That's all there is to say, right?

00:08:06.260 --> 00:08:11.100
It's not you who wants to meet X,
it's that heart's owner.

00:08:11.100 --> 00:08:14.310
It's a memory from another lifetime
that has nothing to do with you--

00:08:14.310 --> 00:08:19.440
No, it's not! It's not just a memory--
it's unfinished business!

00:08:19.440 --> 00:08:22.480
Even after their body died and
they passed this heart over to me,

00:08:22.480 --> 00:08:24.860
they still want to see
this person that much!

00:08:24.860 --> 00:08:29.740
I received life from this heart,
so I want to pay back the favor.

00:08:29.740 --> 00:08:33.450
I want to let this heart meet X.

00:08:33.450 --> 00:08:35.080
It's just for your own satisfaction.

00:08:35.080 --> 00:08:37.330
That's right, it's for
my own satisfaction.

00:08:37.330 --> 00:08:41.330
This heart is mine.
So I want to meet them!

00:08:41.330 --> 00:08:43.880
This contradicts what
you were saying before.

00:08:43.880 --> 00:08:45.500
Hush!

00:08:49.300 --> 00:08:50.970
In any case, help me.

00:08:50.970 --> 00:08:53.510
I assume I'm going to be compensated...

00:08:53.510 --> 00:08:57.140
As far as that goes, I let you touch
my chest as advance payment, didn't I?

00:08:57.140 --> 00:08:59.520
Talk about a high-pressure pitch...

00:09:06.110 --> 00:09:07.740
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:09:15.410 --> 00:09:21.080
You shouldn't ogle a girl from your grade
who's not your girlfriend like that.

00:09:21.080 --> 00:09:24.500
You're one to talk, after pressing a guy
from your grade--not your boyfriend--

00:09:24.500 --> 00:09:27.250
against your boobs.

00:09:27.250 --> 00:09:29.840
You know you enjoyed it.

00:09:34.050 --> 00:09:36.970
Honestly, you're staring too much.

00:09:37.930 --> 00:09:43.400
No, I wasn't--I was taking a look at
your, um, collarbones, not your chest.

00:09:43.400 --> 00:09:47.730
That's scary! I'd rather that
you'd been looking at my chest.

00:09:47.730 --> 00:09:51.070
For your age, Natsunagi,
you have great collarbones.

00:09:51.070 --> 00:09:54.910
I have no idea what connection you think
there is between age and collarbones!

00:09:55.950 --> 00:09:58.950
Hmm, haven't we gone through
a back-and-forth like this before?

00:09:58.950 --> 00:10:01.620
The thought of a conversation
like this happening more than once

00:10:01.620 --> 00:10:03.620
is beyond hellish.

00:10:03.620 --> 00:10:06.340
Well, shall we get going--?

00:10:07.340 --> 00:10:09.670
Grab that guy! He's a thief!

00:10:09.670 --> 00:10:10.960
Eh?

00:10:15.300 --> 00:10:16.550
Wha--?

00:10:18.430 --> 00:10:22.270
Yeesh... you again,
you little piece of crap?

00:10:25.730 --> 00:10:30.110
You're mixed up in about three-quarters
of the crimes in this district.

00:10:30.110 --> 00:10:33.400
It's just something in my nature.

00:10:33.400 --> 00:10:36.570
And? You're working on your own now?

00:10:36.570 --> 00:10:39.990
No, by myself I'm of no use,
especially against--

00:10:39.990 --> 00:10:44.000
Also, it seems as though
I'm off the radar for that crew.

00:10:44.000 --> 00:10:49.420
Ha, you're quite the cold-hearted one.
"The dead tell no tales," eh?

00:10:51.090 --> 00:10:53.760
Ow! What was that for?

00:10:53.760 --> 00:10:57.850
Just felt like the thing to do.
Or should I say...?

00:10:57.850 --> 00:11:00.890
All right. This is Fuubi-<i>san</i>.

00:11:02.520 --> 00:11:04.520
Fuubi Kase.

00:11:04.520 --> 00:11:07.230
You're a police person, right?

00:11:07.230 --> 00:11:12.480
She's an assistant inspector, supposedly.
This is who we were going to meet.

00:11:12.480 --> 00:11:13.610
Eh?

00:11:13.610 --> 00:11:17.280
Fuubi-<i>san</i>, there's something about
my girl here that I want to discuss.

00:11:17.280 --> 00:11:18.070
She's your girl?

00:11:18.070 --> 00:11:20.160
It's just an expression.

00:11:20.160 --> 00:11:24.410
Pleased to meet you.
My name is Nagisa Natsunagi.

00:11:24.410 --> 00:11:29.210
Something to discuss... Why with me?

00:11:29.210 --> 00:11:32.090
Knowing you, I thought
you could do something.

00:11:32.090 --> 00:11:35.550
Idiot. What is it you think I could do?

00:11:35.550 --> 00:11:39.640
Fuubi-<i>san</i>, you're different
from normal police.

00:11:39.640 --> 00:11:42.430
Different? How?

00:11:42.430 --> 00:11:44.140
Your resolve.

00:11:49.480 --> 00:11:55.990
I see. I get what you're saying.
But we're not doctors.

00:11:55.990 --> 00:11:57.650
Take it up with someone else.

00:11:57.650 --> 00:12:00.030
Please! I can't help wanting to--

00:12:00.030 --> 00:12:02.120
What's more...

00:12:02.120 --> 00:12:08.040
I'm busy. After this, I'm scheduled to put
in an appearance at the big house.

00:12:08.040 --> 00:12:09.880
The big house...

00:12:11.090 --> 00:12:16.420
Now... if you two were to take it
upon yourselves to tag along...

00:12:16.420 --> 00:12:18.680
...that's up to you.

00:12:24.390 --> 00:12:28.940
Listen, I've got some work
to wrap up upstairs.

00:12:28.940 --> 00:12:32.190
I'll be headed out in 20 minutes,
so keep that in mind.

00:12:35.480 --> 00:12:36.990
You understand?

00:12:36.990 --> 00:12:38.320
Yes, ma'am.

00:12:40.570 --> 00:12:47.160
Umm, Kimizuka, it's too late to ask,
but weren't we going to some big house?

00:12:47.160 --> 00:12:49.670
This place is very clearly...

00:12:49.670 --> 00:12:51.080
It's a prison, I'd say.

00:12:51.080 --> 00:12:54.840
What's this, "I'd say"? What happened to
the big house we were going to visit?

00:12:54.840 --> 00:12:56.920
It's slang! Slang!

00:12:56.920 --> 00:12:58.510
S-Slang?

00:12:58.510 --> 00:13:00.590
Why do you get so worked up?

00:13:00.590 --> 00:13:01.550
Eh?

00:13:01.550 --> 00:13:07.060
Let's go. Where we're headed...
is all the way at the end.

00:13:10.810 --> 00:13:12.350
Who's here?

00:13:12.350 --> 00:13:13.360
A guy.

00:13:13.360 --> 00:13:14.820
Be serious.

00:13:14.820 --> 00:13:16.900
A guy who gave up on being human.

00:13:16.900 --> 00:13:19.860
Would you...? Huh?

00:13:23.570 --> 00:13:29.750
Oh-ho. It's been quite a while...
legendary detective.

00:13:29.750 --> 00:13:33.630
Unfortunately, I'm no legendary detective.

00:13:34.790 --> 00:13:40.420
No, you were... Ah, Watson, right?

00:13:40.420 --> 00:13:44.050
Can those eyes of yours see anything?

00:13:44.050 --> 00:13:49.220
Nope. I'm just like you now, Watson--
with those dead-fish eyes of yours.

00:13:49.220 --> 00:13:56.570
That's the tragedy of the century.
Also, you can stop calling me that.

00:13:56.570 --> 00:14:00.320
What, did you give up
the sidekick business?

00:14:06.870 --> 00:14:09.620
We came today to talk
to you about something.

00:14:09.620 --> 00:14:11.870
You wouldn't have come
to this place to see me

00:14:11.870 --> 00:14:15.580
if there wasn't some special circumstance.

00:14:15.580 --> 00:14:20.800
This is a perfect way to kill some time.
Tell me about it.

00:14:20.800 --> 00:14:22.300
I see...

00:14:23.590 --> 00:14:25.220
What's wrong?

00:14:26.350 --> 00:14:30.600
You seem very nervous. That's unlike you.

00:14:30.600 --> 00:14:32.680
What's that supposed to mean?

00:14:36.110 --> 00:14:38.570
Bat, I'll introduce you.

00:14:38.570 --> 00:14:43.240
The girl beside me is Nagisa Natsunagi;
we're in the same year at school.

00:14:43.240 --> 00:14:47.320
Nagisa... Natsunagi?

00:14:47.320 --> 00:14:51.040
Nice to meet you. My name is Natsunagi.

00:14:51.040 --> 00:14:57.170
I... came today to talk
to you about my heart.

00:15:08.760 --> 00:15:15.390
I see. You're asking if I happen to know
anything about that heart's owner?

00:15:15.390 --> 00:15:20.190
Yes, that's right. That's it, but...

00:15:20.190 --> 00:15:24.570
Natsunagi, he's not a guy with what
you'd call an ordinary background.

00:15:24.570 --> 00:15:28.490
And while I'm at it, let's say he's
also no ordinary human being.

00:15:28.490 --> 00:15:29.700
Eh?

00:15:29.700 --> 00:15:35.710
Bat is a partial android--produced
by the covert organization SPES.

00:15:35.710 --> 00:15:37.000
Excuse me?

00:15:37.000 --> 00:15:38.750
It's not believable, huh?

00:15:38.750 --> 00:15:41.460
Of course it's not,
that kind of ridiculous talk--

00:15:41.460 --> 00:15:46.760
In this great big world,
such things do exist.

00:15:49.180 --> 00:15:54.140
If I choose to, I can hear people
talking 100 kilometers away.

00:15:54.140 --> 00:15:58.810
It's no challenge at all to make out
the sound of your heart, young missy.

00:15:58.810 --> 00:16:02.020
This piece of work jet-setted around
the world, using that thing as a weapon.

00:16:02.020 --> 00:16:04.940
So I thought there was a chance

00:16:04.940 --> 00:16:10.070
that he might have encountered
your heart's previous owner.

00:16:10.070 --> 00:16:15.620
I wasn't trying to hide anything from you,
but I know this man well.

00:16:15.620 --> 00:16:18.830
Seems like it.

00:16:18.830 --> 00:16:24.420
Has it been four years already
since I had that scrape with you two?

00:16:24.420 --> 00:16:26.420
You... two?

00:16:26.420 --> 00:16:28.680
Such nostalgia I'm feeling.

00:16:28.680 --> 00:16:33.970
So, yeah, I don't want that ear
listening to the sound of my heart.

00:16:33.970 --> 00:16:35.890
That's understandable...

00:16:35.890 --> 00:16:41.020
Oh, come on. To hear the sound of your
heart, this distance is near enough.

00:16:41.020 --> 00:16:46.240
Or should I say, I've already discerned
everything about your heart, missy.

00:16:46.240 --> 00:16:47.740
Huh?

00:16:47.740 --> 00:16:54.580
Bat... have you really met the owner
of Natsunagi's heart before?

00:16:54.580 --> 00:16:59.620
In place of a tedious explanation,
doing this will be quicker!

00:17:04.420 --> 00:17:06.260
Does this mean...?

00:17:13.930 --> 00:17:15.850
Siesta!

00:17:15.850 --> 00:17:20.350
You'll never be able to raise
an appendage against me again.

00:17:20.350 --> 00:17:24.400
I was just born to be a legendary
detective; it's in my nature.

00:17:26.230 --> 00:17:33.490
It can't be... That's...
That's not... Don't do this to me.

00:17:34.450 --> 00:17:35.620
I'm no longer--

00:17:35.620 --> 00:17:39.960
Watson... burying your head
in the sand is pathetic.

00:17:41.210 --> 00:17:46.500
From the beginning, I was sure it was
that other girl who had come here.

00:17:48.550 --> 00:17:53.550
It's been quite a while...
legendary detective.

00:17:54.890 --> 00:18:00.850
So that's what this is about.
I thought it was weird.

00:18:00.850 --> 00:18:07.360
I was never the type to hug a guy I was
meeting for the first time or anything.

00:18:07.360 --> 00:18:13.860
So that behavior wasn't me;
it had to be the owner of this heart.

00:18:13.860 --> 00:18:15.910
It was something that girl made me do--

00:18:15.910 --> 00:18:20.000
the legendary detective Siesta,
whose sidekick you were.

00:18:20.000 --> 00:18:23.580
Natsunagi, you...

00:18:27.460 --> 00:18:29.840
It's a coincidence.

00:18:29.840 --> 00:18:35.800
Meeting you, and the fact that
Siesta's heart is inside you...

00:18:35.800 --> 00:18:38.060
It's all just a...

00:18:44.100 --> 00:18:48.480
Is that the influence of your heart's
former owner, too, Natsunagi?

00:18:48.480 --> 00:18:55.200
It's not. That was my intention.
I wanted to hit you, so I hit you!

00:18:55.200 --> 00:18:59.080
A coincidence? You call this
reunion a coincidence?

00:18:59.080 --> 00:19:03.500
What a joke! Don't try to brush this
under the rug with that word!

00:19:03.500 --> 00:19:09.960
This is a yearning! Even after dying,
wanting to see you, to be with you!

00:19:09.960 --> 00:19:18.430
It's this little heart's one and
only wish! For a long time, we--

00:19:18.430 --> 00:19:22.390
Kimihiko Kimizuka,
I've been searching for you!

00:19:22.390 --> 00:19:27.190
Don't try to sew it all up with
the words "just a coincidence"!

00:19:27.190 --> 00:19:30.570
Don't you dare make light
of someone's heart's desire!

00:19:36.160 --> 00:19:38.240
Are you in there?

00:19:40.530 --> 00:19:46.210
Do you know the suffering I went through
after becoming your sidekick...?

00:19:46.210 --> 00:19:50.590
A battle with a supernatural organization
ensued, and for three years,

00:19:50.590 --> 00:19:54.090
in desperate straits, we traveled the
world evading pursuers, penniless.

00:19:54.090 --> 00:19:57.510
We slept outdoors in a hurricane.

00:19:57.510 --> 00:19:59.220
On one occasion,
after winning in a casino,

00:19:59.220 --> 00:20:02.350
we jumped up and down
on a resort hotel bed,

00:20:02.350 --> 00:20:05.100
but of course, the very next day,
we were broke again.

00:20:05.100 --> 00:20:07.900
We walked through deserts,
traversed jungles,

00:20:07.900 --> 00:20:10.310
passed over mountains, and crossed oceans.

00:20:10.310 --> 00:20:13.820
And then... And then...

00:20:15.610 --> 00:20:20.160
How could you die before me? You fool.

00:20:34.710 --> 00:20:40.220
I'm glad it was fruitful.
Feel free to thank me all you want.

00:20:40.220 --> 00:20:43.850
Fuubi-<i>san</i>, you knew from
the start, didn't you?

00:20:43.850 --> 00:20:45.810
Huh?

00:20:45.810 --> 00:20:52.020
About her... About who Natsunagi's
heart once belonged to.

00:20:53.150 --> 00:20:54.690
Fuubi-<i>san</i>.

00:21:01.910 --> 00:21:06.700
I'd never be cruel enough to demand
the young lady do detective work.

00:21:14.130 --> 00:21:16.460
Thanks for today.

00:21:16.460 --> 00:21:17.800
Eh?

00:21:17.800 --> 00:21:22.050
Thanks to you...
how do I put this, it's...

00:21:22.050 --> 00:21:26.390
I couldn't go on as I was--
that's what I realized.

00:21:26.390 --> 00:21:29.690
If you're saying that, then I also...

00:21:34.060 --> 00:21:40.570
Natsunagi... whomever
that heart may belong to,

00:21:40.570 --> 00:21:44.620
you can live your own life.

00:21:44.620 --> 00:21:46.660
Oh...

00:21:46.660 --> 00:21:50.290
You don't need to try to replace anybody.

00:21:52.880 --> 00:21:54.330
See you around.

00:21:57.960 --> 00:22:00.920
Kimizuka, I--

00:22:02.180 --> 00:22:04.470
What is it, Natsunagi?

00:22:06.180 --> 00:22:07.810
Umm, I...

00:22:07.810 --> 00:22:09.890
Huh?

00:22:09.890 --> 00:22:14.440
There's something I'd like to ask
a legendary detective to handle!

00:23:45.020 --> 00:23:50.030
Episode 3

00:23:45.020 --> 00:23:50.030
That's Yui-nya Quality
